40
00:05:21,240 --> 00:05:23,700
Abandoned on the doorstep when they were only babies.

41
00:05:24,020 --> 00:05:25,240
And now look at them.

42
00:05:25,500 --> 00:05:27,200
With the money they've sent home every month,

43
00:05:27,280 --> 00:05:29,680
we fixed up the church and laid in enough pot potatoes

44
00:05:29,680 --> 00:05:31,800
to keep everybody's stomachs full this winter.

45
00:05:32,700 --> 00:05:33,900
Here is this.

46
00:05:34,680 --> 00:05:35,720
Perfect, thanks.

47
00:05:35,720 --> 00:05:41,140
Here you go.

48
00:05:41,160 --> 00:05:42,180
Why don't you keep it?

49
00:05:43,440 --> 00:05:44,500
Are you sure?

50
00:05:44,700 --> 00:05:46,720
In this world, magic is everything.

51
00:05:47,260 --> 00:05:50,300
So what could ever become of a boy who has none?

52
00:05:53,520 --> 00:05:58,520
Now, never once has anyone from this region distinguished him or herself

53
00:05:58,520 --> 00:06:01,740
by becoming a magic knight, much less the wizard king.

54
00:06:01,740 --> 00:06:04,680
I pray that one among you will have what it takes

55
00:06:04,680 --> 00:06:07,040
to become the most powerful mage in the land.

56
00:06:07,040 --> 00:06:13,780
And now, to accept your grimoires.

57
00:06:26,480 --> 00:06:28,520
Finally, my very own grimoire.

58
00:06:28,520 --> 00:06:33,320
You know, was given the legendary four-leaf clover grimoire.

59
00:06:39,320 --> 00:06:42,080
I will become the wizard king.

60
00:06:42,420 --> 00:06:45,520
But, as for the magic-less Asta...

61
00:06:46,300 --> 00:06:47,520
Hey, uh...

62
00:06:47,520 --> 00:06:52,500
Is my grimoire running late or something?

63
00:06:56,380 --> 00:07:00,080
Now, time for a hearty swig of magic-boosting mogul leaf juice.

64
00:07:00,280 --> 00:07:00,940
Bottoms up!

65
00:07:04,980 --> 00:07:05,300
Ah!

66
00:07:09,300 --> 00:07:11,300
Oh, wow.

67
00:07:11,520 --> 00:07:12,160
You're kidding.

68
00:07:12,500 --> 00:07:14,000
That's actually kind of awesome.

69
00:07:14,060 --> 00:07:14,200
What?

70
00:07:14,200 --> 00:07:16,260
You don't have any magic!

71
00:07:16,560 --> 00:07:19,420
How could you get a grimoire and that sword?

72
00:07:19,620 --> 00:07:22,300
What kind of freak of nature are you?

73
00:07:24,680 --> 00:07:25,120
Ah!

74
00:07:29,760 --> 00:07:30,400
Yeah!

75
00:07:33,420 --> 00:07:37,780
You took my spell and turned it into your magic power?

76
00:07:39,880 --> 00:07:40,240
Yeah!

77
00:07:40,240 --> 00:07:44,180
Even without traditional magic power,

78
00:07:44,600 --> 00:07:46,780
I will be the wizard king!

79
00:07:47,020 --> 00:07:49,800
My magic is never giving up!

80
00:07:49,860 --> 00:07:50,660
Ah!

81
00:07:58,660 --> 00:07:59,920
Well, what do you think?

82
00:08:00,100 --> 00:08:01,480
My very own grimoire!

83
00:08:01,900 --> 00:08:04,200
I don't know how it happened, but I got one!

84
00:08:04,200 --> 00:08:09,900
Sounds like he's holding his own.

85
00:08:10,980 --> 00:08:14,160
Juno, Asta, my boys!

86
00:08:14,400 --> 00:08:15,800
You're the bride of the village!

87
00:08:15,980 --> 00:08:16,860
Thank you, father.

88
00:08:16,860 --> 00:08:39,220
The first time I saw Asta was on the day of the Magic Night's entrance exam.

89
00:08:39,220 --> 00:08:44,220
Even then, there isn't any. He's sparkled.

90
00:08:54,220 --> 00:08:58,220
Ha ha ha! One of us is gonna be the Wizard King!

91
00:08:58,220 --> 00:09:01,220
This is where our legend begins! Right, you know?

92
00:09:01,220 --> 00:09:04,220
I've been training for this the last six months!

93
00:09:04,220 --> 00:09:06,220
Wait, will you see what I can do?

94
00:09:06,220 --> 00:09:09,220
Why are they trying to kill me?!

95
00:09:09,220 --> 00:09:11,220
What the hell?

96
00:09:11,220 --> 00:09:15,220
Poor schmuck. Not the nicest welcome to the big city.

97
00:09:15,220 --> 00:09:19,220
Get the hell away from me!

98
00:09:23,220 --> 00:09:27,220
One of them. A real Magic Knight squad captain.

99
00:09:27,220 --> 00:09:38,220
On to the next test. The final and most difficult. A display of combat skill.

100
00:09:38,220 --> 00:09:42,220
As Knight's battle is our business, we want to see everything you're capable of!

101
00:09:42,220 --> 00:09:46,220
The best way to show off now is to pair off with someone strong!

102
00:09:46,220 --> 00:09:48,220
Ha ha! What do you say you and I pair up?

103
00:09:48,220 --> 00:09:55,220
Do you really mean it, Seke? You're willing to take on a charity case like me?

104
00:09:58,220 --> 00:10:03,220
We're both working for the same goal. So we'll have a fair fight, but nobody pulls any punches, okay?

105
00:10:03,220 --> 00:10:05,220
No! Begin!

106
00:10:05,220 --> 00:10:08,220
No pulling punches, remember?

107
00:10:08,220 --> 00:10:11,220
Let's do this, Asta! Ha ha!

108
00:10:16,220 --> 00:10:20,220
Bronze Creation Magic! Seke Magnum Cannonball!

109
00:10:20,220 --> 00:10:22,220
Come on, don't get shy on me now!

110
00:10:22,220 --> 00:10:23,220
Ha ha!

111
00:10:23,220 --> 00:10:25,220
Okay, here we go.

112
00:10:25,220 --> 00:10:26,220
Here we go.

113
00:10:42,220 --> 00:10:47,220
Unlike you, Seke, I'm not joining the Magic Knights just so I can slack off and have a little fun!

114
00:10:48,220 --> 00:10:52,220
I've got a much bigger goal! I'm gonna be the Wizard King!

115
00:10:52,220 --> 00:10:55,220
So cool...

116
00:11:09,220 --> 00:11:11,220
It's like magic is coming off him in waves!

117
00:11:12,220 --> 00:11:15,220
This is it! The power of a Magic Knight captain!

118
00:11:16,220 --> 00:11:21,220
What you said before? That you took the exam because you want to become the Wizard King?

119
00:11:22,220 --> 00:11:27,220
And now, standing here magicless and pathetic, can you really say you have what it takes?

120
00:11:28,220 --> 00:11:30,220
That you're strong enough to be the Wizard King?

121
00:11:34,220 --> 00:11:38,220
Yeah, fine. So maybe I won't get to join a Magic Knight squad today.

122
00:11:38,220 --> 00:11:48,220
But no matter what anyone says, and no matter how many times I might stumble, I won't give up! I will become the Wizard King!

123
00:11:48,220 --> 00:11:49,220
Wizard King!

124
00:11:49,220 --> 00:11:51,220
You know, kid, I like you! Come join our crew!

125
00:11:51,220 --> 00:11:52,220
What?

126
00:11:52,220 --> 00:11:55,220
Quit gaping like a fish! I'm saying I'll let you into the Black Bulls!

127
00:11:55,220 --> 00:11:57,220
I wasn't the only one who saw the bright glow of Asta's inner light. The captain did, too. And that's the story about Asta's inner light.

128
00:11:57,220 --> 00:11:59,220
And that's the story of how Asta came to join the Black Bulls family.

129
00:11:59,220 --> 00:12:03,220
And let's not forget Asta's childhood friend. He was the only one who saw the bright glow of Asta's inner light. The captain did, too.

130
00:12:03,220 --> 00:12:13,220
And that's the story of how Asta came to join the Black Bulls family. Let's not forget Asta's childhood friend, Yuno.

131
00:12:30,220 --> 00:12:31,220
Do we have any hands?

132
00:12:33,220 --> 00:12:39,220
No way? All of them? Impossible!

133
00:12:39,220 --> 00:12:42,220
Has that ever happened?

134
00:12:42,220 --> 00:12:46,220
I guess it's not just royalty and nobles who can get into the Golden Dawn.

135
00:12:46,220 --> 00:12:50,220
Whoa! They all want him? Way to show him, Yuno!

136
00:12:54,220 --> 00:13:02,220
I have to choose the squad that offers me the best path to becoming the Wizard King. It would be an honor to join the Golden Dawn.

137
00:13:03,220 --> 00:13:04,220
What?

138
00:13:04,220 --> 00:13:05,220
What?

139
00:13:07,220 --> 00:13:16,220
Asta and I are basically brothers now. So any childhood friend of his is a childhood friend of mine. In other words, Yuno and I are best friends.

140
00:13:16,220 --> 00:13:17,220
Hmm.

141
00:13:20,220 --> 00:13:25,220
Now then, time for today's entry in my observation diary.

142
00:13:27,220 --> 00:13:32,220
Today, my dearish friend Asta worked his very hardest, just like he does at the time.

143
00:13:32,220 --> 00:13:33,220
What?

144
00:13:33,220 --> 00:13:34,220
What?

145
00:13:34,220 --> 00:13:35,220
What?

146
00:13:35,220 --> 00:13:36,220
What?

147
00:13:36,220 --> 00:13:37,220
What?

148
00:13:37,220 --> 00:13:38,220
What?

149
00:13:38,220 --> 00:13:39,220
What?

150
00:13:39,220 --> 00:13:40,220
What?

151
00:13:40,220 --> 00:13:42,220
What?

152
00:13:42,220 --> 00:13:43,220
Oh!

153
00:13:43,220 --> 00:13:44,220
What?

154
00:13:44,220 --> 00:13:45,220
What?

155
00:13:49,220 --> 00:13:51,220
What?

156
00:13:51,220 --> 00:13:56,080
No! My heart belongs to Sister Lily, and I won't betray her for anybody!

157
00:13:58,780 --> 00:13:59,300
Next!

158
00:14:06,260 --> 00:14:09,420
Sit, Beastie!

159
00:14:11,140 --> 00:14:14,380
There. Good boy. I think you've earned a treat.

160
00:14:14,380 --> 00:14:21,860
What are you doing, you slobbery mutt? Let me go! I'm not your dinner!

161
00:14:27,380 --> 00:14:32,440
It's so hot! I mean, maybe it is for a normal person, but this heat should be nothing to a black ball.

162
00:14:33,620 --> 00:14:35,520
What's wrong? Do you want to get out already?

163
00:14:36,080 --> 00:14:39,060
No, of course not! I can stay in! I'm not done yet!

164
00:14:39,060 --> 00:14:58,060
Honestly, does he have a death wish? You're with me on this one, right, Nero? He's just so... so reckless.

165
00:14:59,060 --> 00:15:04,800
And he's been that way since our very first mission. That ridiculous boar hunt.

166
00:15:04,800 --> 00:15:20,980
We barely made it to Saucy Village when we were accosted by a band of thugs.

167
00:15:26,660 --> 00:15:27,580
Hey, Asta!

168
00:15:27,740 --> 00:15:27,940
Sir!

169
00:15:27,940 --> 00:15:28,040
Sir!

170
00:15:28,040 --> 00:15:29,040
Sir!

171
00:15:40,040 --> 00:15:41,000
Kill them.

172
00:15:50,360 --> 00:15:51,220
Think again!

173
00:15:51,720 --> 00:15:52,600
Sure!

174
00:15:52,600 --> 00:15:59,080
Do you imagine you can still protect your herd of beasts like this?

175
00:16:01,080 --> 00:16:01,640
Cluster!

176
00:16:02,300 --> 00:16:03,140
Too late.

177
00:16:13,200 --> 00:16:16,040
You stand no chance of prevailing against me.

178
00:16:16,600 --> 00:16:18,300
Why not accept that and give up?

179
00:16:18,640 --> 00:16:22,120
If I gave up now, then who would protect them?

180
00:16:23,360 --> 00:16:25,120
I realized something.

181
00:16:26,580 --> 00:16:29,160
Sooner or later, I'm going to be the Wizard King.

182
00:16:29,700 --> 00:16:31,860
But it's not just about keeping a promise.

183
00:16:32,360 --> 00:16:34,040
It's about keeping people safe!

184
00:16:36,240 --> 00:16:37,940
Wizard King might fight!

185
00:16:38,320 --> 00:16:41,000
What does he think would have happened if I hadn't been there?

186
00:16:42,220 --> 00:16:45,480
Well, I did mentally cheer for him, but still...

187
00:16:45,480 --> 00:16:47,040
It's not like that means anything.

188
00:16:47,440 --> 00:16:48,260
Not really.

189
00:16:49,260 --> 00:16:50,880
This has to stop!

190
00:16:51,000 --> 00:16:52,040
It's not like that!

191
00:16:52,040 --> 00:16:54,780
I mean, me and that idiot commoner?

192
00:16:54,980 --> 00:16:55,920
There's no way!

193
00:16:56,040 --> 00:16:56,980
I'm royalty!

194
00:16:57,880 --> 00:16:59,740
And he's basically a lunatic.

195
00:17:00,820 --> 00:17:02,180
Like back in the dungeon.

196
00:17:03,180 --> 00:17:04,400
Your new opponent!

197
00:17:04,400 --> 00:17:07,540
He's right here!

198
00:17:07,540 --> 00:17:07,580
He's right here!

199
00:17:14,180 --> 00:17:15,540
What for me?

200
00:17:15,980 --> 00:17:17,180
Be gone, boy!

201
00:17:17,180 --> 00:17:25,880
Why are you just sitting there, Insect?

202
00:17:26,880 --> 00:17:27,680
You're awake!

203
00:17:28,040 --> 00:17:28,980
Now get moving.

204
00:17:29,560 --> 00:17:31,720
And don't you dare give up until you beat him.

205
00:17:32,400 --> 00:17:32,880
Understand?

206
00:17:32,880 --> 00:17:33,100
Understand?

207
00:17:33,100 --> 00:17:33,880
Yeah.

208
00:17:33,880 --> 00:17:44,080
I'll bring this guy down, and I'll get one or two hits in for you while I'm at it.

209
00:17:44,080 --> 00:17:45,200
Give up.

210
00:17:45,740 --> 00:17:46,800
You can't win.

211
00:17:47,340 --> 00:17:49,080
I live to destroy the weak.

212
00:17:49,620 --> 00:17:51,620
Well, you're not going to destroy me!

213
00:17:51,620 --> 00:17:58,080
I may not have any magic power, but what I do have are my friends!

214
00:17:58,080 --> 00:18:10,820
I don't really know how, but I did it.

215
00:18:10,820 --> 00:18:23,860
I'm dead.

216
00:18:25,160 --> 00:18:26,440
What's happening?

217
00:18:28,480 --> 00:18:29,700
Let's die!

218
00:18:32,960 --> 00:18:35,460
Even if he was fine in the end.

219
00:18:38,060 --> 00:18:40,040
Might be dead if it weren't for you.

220
00:18:40,820 --> 00:18:41,800
Thanks a lot.

221
00:18:42,320 --> 00:18:43,860
I'm so very sorry!

222
00:18:54,560 --> 00:18:56,280
You were really great back there.

223
00:18:56,520 --> 00:18:57,600
Thank you so much.

224
00:18:57,760 --> 00:18:58,480
No problem.

225
00:18:58,900 --> 00:19:01,040
Sorry I kind of ruined the mixer for you.

226
00:19:01,340 --> 00:19:02,180
You didn't, though.

227
00:19:04,860 --> 00:19:05,880
Hey, Asta?

228
00:19:07,160 --> 00:19:10,800
Do you have anyone who's special to you?

229
00:19:11,240 --> 00:19:11,680
Yes!

230
00:19:11,800 --> 00:19:13,360
I've got my heart set on someone!

231
00:19:15,740 --> 00:19:17,040
Someone's special, huh?

232
00:19:17,660 --> 00:19:19,580
Someone he's got his heart set on.

233
00:19:19,920 --> 00:19:22,280
If he cares so much, he shouldn't make me worry.

234
00:19:22,720 --> 00:19:23,700
Who's making you worry?

235
00:19:24,700 --> 00:19:26,740
How long have you been there anyway?

236
00:19:26,740 --> 00:19:28,720
It isn't nice to sneak up on people!

237
00:19:29,080 --> 00:19:29,900
Not long.

238
00:19:30,000 --> 00:19:32,000
I just got back from an epic training session.

239
00:19:32,500 --> 00:19:33,720
What are you up to in here?

240
00:19:33,720 --> 00:19:47,520
We've been given a mission of grave importance.

241
00:19:47,860 --> 00:19:48,860
Right, we're ready.

242
00:19:48,860 --> 00:19:53,000
You know, perhaps it would be best if you stayed behind.

243
00:19:53,360 --> 00:19:54,720
If your injuries aren't healed...

244
00:19:54,720 --> 00:19:55,540
I'll be fine.

245
00:19:56,620 --> 00:19:59,720
It's so sweet of you to put Yuno's health first like that.

246
00:19:59,900 --> 00:20:01,040
I am not sweet.

247
00:20:01,580 --> 00:20:04,400
Bringing along an injured man would slow us down, that's all.

248
00:20:04,800 --> 00:20:07,280
My concern is for the mission, not Yuno's health.

249
00:20:07,720 --> 00:20:08,220
Let's go.

250
00:20:08,220 --> 00:20:12,180
You're not riding?

251
00:20:13,040 --> 00:20:14,680
Well, uh...

252
00:20:14,680 --> 00:20:16,600
It's just more of a broom sort of day.

253
00:20:17,060 --> 00:20:17,500
You know?

254
00:20:18,560 --> 00:20:19,540
Don't be shy.

255
00:20:20,220 --> 00:20:23,000
It doesn't use too much magic power if that's what you're worried about.

256
00:20:23,560 --> 00:20:24,800
Oh, I'm not being shy.

257
00:20:25,340 --> 00:20:29,740
And I'm definitely not thinking about how embarrassing it would be if my friend saw me riding in that.

258
00:20:30,040 --> 00:20:30,520
Yeah.

259
00:20:31,080 --> 00:20:32,140
Now see here!

260
00:20:32,400 --> 00:20:34,240
Are you two making fun of my chariot?

261
00:20:34,240 --> 00:20:35,420
Of course not.

262
00:20:36,320 --> 00:20:36,880
Hey!

263
00:20:37,160 --> 00:20:37,920
Come back!

264
00:20:38,200 --> 00:20:40,000
You can't take off on your own like that!

265
00:20:42,640 --> 00:20:44,540
Well, I'll just be on my way too then!

266
00:20:46,640 --> 00:20:48,940
I can't waste any time resting.

267
00:20:49,560 --> 00:20:51,320
